    <GaugingStation location="Upper Monachyle" name="Monachyle Burn" number="18023">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">One of the Balquhidder experimental catchments.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Containable head 1.2m has max. flow of 9.0 cumecs.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Aluminium alloy Flat V (1:10) weir, 3.2m wide with vertical sidewalls, keyed into a natural rockbar. Station added to peak flows dataset in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Instrumentation problems throughout 1996, data infilled from Lower Monachyle and Kirkton.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Very wet interfluve area to the break in slope to a steep- sided glacial valley. Shallow and deep peat, peaty gleys and upland brown earths over mica schist. Some bare rock on W boundary. Heather moorland. Experimental catchment run by IH, nested within 18017 and neighbouring 18018.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Flows based on weir equation only." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Flows based on weir equation only." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
